  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sheetal Dhariwal vs Union Of India & Ors. on 30 April, 2024 Author: Manmeet Pritam Singh Arora Bench: Manmeet Pritam Singh Arora $~33 * In The High Court Of Delhi At New Delhi + W.P.(C) 6039/2024 Sheetal Dhariwal .... Through: Mr. Chandan Bhatia a Kumar Singh, Advocat Versus Union Of India & Ors. .. Through: Mr. Kirtiman Singh, Waize Ali Noor, Mr. Mr. Varun P. Singh, Baijal, Mr. Aryan Ag Shreya V. Mehra, Adv Mr. Rishabh Srivasta Singh, Mr. Pradyumn Mr.Vikas Saini, Advo Santosh Kumar Tripat Counsel for Gnctd, R Mr. Rakesh Chaudhary Sushaar Chaudhary, A R-3 Mr. Aditya Singla, A with Mr. Ritvik Saha Garg and Mr. Raghav Advocates for R-3 % Date of Decision: Coram: Hon'Ble The Acting Chief Justice Hon'Ble Ms. Justice Manmeet Pritam Singh Arora Judgment",
    "facts": "Present public interest petition petition, which is fourth in a series of petition, filed by the Petitioner seek seeks compliance with Regulation 2.3.4 of the Food Safety and Standards (Prohibition and Restrictions on Sales) Regulations, 2011 (for short '2011 2011 Regulations') Sheetal Dhariwal vs Union Of India & Ors. on 30 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/51658165/ 1 Regulations ) which prohibits use of tobacco and nicotine as ingredients in any food product including pan masala masala. 2. The second petition bearing W.P.(C) No. 3208/2024 was dismissed vide order dated 04th March,, 2024 on account of absence of relevant empirical data showing usage of tobacco and nicotine as ingredients in pan masala and due to non-impleadment adment of necessary parties. Thereafter, the third petition being W.P.(C) No. 4077/2024 /2024 filed by the Petitioner seeking identical prayers was disposed of vide order dated 18th March, 2024 with directions to the Food Safety and Standards Authority of India ('FSSAI')) to treat the writ petition as a representation and to decide the same in accordance with law after giving an opportunity of hearing to the Petitioner. 3.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the Petitioner states that the Petitioner has not received any response to her representation in accordance with the order dated 18th March, 2024. 4. Learned counsel for the FSSAI, who appears on advance notice notice, states that the Petitioner representation's is under consideration.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the Petitioner states that the Petitioner has not received any response to her representation in accordance with the order dated 18th March, 2024. 4. Learned counsel for the FSSAI, who appears on advance notice notice, states that the Petitioner representation's is under consideration.",
